                                "sense_id": "f5d13c4a-6f34-337d-a322-2dd7b6c8aa81",
                                "text": "In India, too, people now wish to bring that argument to a close: to replace the ruckus of politics with the moralized ideology of Hindutva."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "b46c543d-9b93-4b29-aab1-4d16aa944e1e",
                                "sense_id": "f5d13c4a-6f34-337d-a322-2dd7b6c8aa81",
                                "text": "China’s one-party meritocracy, Putin’s uncrowned czardom, the post-Arab Spring triumph of dictatorship and monarchy over religious populism in the Middle East, the Hindutva populism transforming Indian democracy — these aren’t just all indistinguishable forms of “autocracy,” but culturally distinctive developments that fit well with Huntington’s typology[…]"
